# Units that exist in this repo and are DELIBERATELY not installed on the Pi.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The off-box backup was written, tested, committed and
# never installed — the units simply did not exist on the box, nothing said so,
# and a month of irreplaceable detections sat on one SD card with no copies while
# a green tree implied otherwise. That is this project's signature failure:
# machinery built carefully and never switched on.
#
# scripts/repo-guards.sh (guard 11c) now fails the build when a unit declares an
# alert path but no installer mentions it. This file is the ONE way to answer
# that guard without installing something — and it costs a written reason, so an
# uninstalled unit is a recorded decision rather than an oversight.
#
# Format: one basename per line, then a reason. Blank lines and # comments
# ignored. Removing a line here means the guard demands an installer.

avian-mqtt.service
#   Forwards detections to an MQTT broker. No broker exists on this LAN and
#   nothing consumes the topic, so installing it would start a service with no
#   listener. Install it the day a broker exists — the unit is ready and now
#   carries the alert path.

weekly_digest.service
#   Pushes a weekly summary to the shared ntfy topic. It is complete and tested,
#   and turning it on is a PRODUCT decision (does the operator want a weekly
#   push?) rather than an engineering one, so it stays off until asked for.
#   Note its own guard: weekly_digest.py refuses to push when derived.json is
#   older than 72h, so it cannot broadcast a stale museum.
